   "List of the shop's products." — the store's product population (the
   authoritative products root the legacy platform roots read — never a
   duplicate store) with its countable-connection envelope (edges/
   pageInfo/totalCount, byte-shape from the pinned schema). These are
   Saleor PUBLIC storefront roots whose include-unpublished variant
   requires MANAGE_ORDERS/MANAGE_DISCOUNTS/MANAGE_PRODUCTS — mapped
   through the platform's ADMIN capability (the SaleorPermissionCatalog
   contract): the public population is the ACTIVE display-lifecycle
   slice; an ADMIN caller's scroll and lookup widen to every state —
   the registered permission-aware population mapping. FORWARD-ONLY
   keyset paging on this first slice: first/after ride the platform's
   REAL SQL keyset scroll (the staffUsers repository-keyset precedent —
   cursors identify a row's sort key (name, id), never an absolute
   offset); before/last stay declared (the exact Saleor argument shape)
   but answer an explicit classified error until a backward scroll
   exists — a recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op. filter
   (deprecated upstream), where, search and channel (no channel model —
   the PENDING-ADR commercial-context row) are likewise the declared
   wire shapes with explicit not-yet-supported errors. The sort
   vocabulary is Saleor's own ProductOrderField enum: NAME (the
   product's own title column) executes as the real keyset sort,
   deterministic with the id tiebreaker; the attributeId sort leg and
   the other thirteen fields answer the explicit not-implemented error.
  """
  products(
    "Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."
    after: String,
    "Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."
    before: String,
    "Slug of a channel for which the data should be returned."
    channel: String,
    "Filtering options for products."
    filter: ProductFilterInput @deprecated(reason : "Use `where` filter instead."),
    "Retrieve the first n elements from the list."
    first: Int,
    "Retrieve the last n elements from the list."
    last: Int,
    "Search products."
    search: String,
    "Sort products."
    sortBy: ProductOrder,
    "Where filtering options for products."
    where: ProductWhereInput
  ): ProductCountableConnection
  """
   "Look up a promotion by ID or external reference." — the Saleor
   promotion lookup (MANAGE_DISCOUNTS → ADMIN here, enforced in the
   owning pricing use case). The id executes through the typed
   global-ID codec: an unknown but well-formed ID answers null (the
   safe absence); a malformed or mistyped global ID answers the
   codec's classified validation error — never a raw UUID fallback.
   externalReference (no external-ID column) stays declared (the
   exact Saleor argument shape) but answers an explicit classified
   error — a recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op.
  """
  promotion(
    "External ID of the promotion (no external-ID column on this platform — an explicit classified error)."
    externalReference: String,
    "ID of the promotion."
    id: ID
  ): Promotion
  """
   "List of the promotions." — the Saleor promotion list with its
   countable-connection envelope (edges/pageInfo/totalCount,
   byte-shape from the pinned schema). FORWARD-ONLY keyset paging on
   this first slice: first/after ride the platform's ScrollPosition
   keyset contract (the staffUsers/permissionGroups/productTypes
   precedent — cursors identify a row's sort key (name|createdAt,
   id), never an absolute offset); before/last stay declared (the
   exact Saleor argument shape) but answer an explicit classified
   error until a backward scroll exists. where is likewise the
   declared wire shape with an explicit not-yet-supported error.
   The sort vocabulary is Saleor's PromotionSortField enum: NAME and
   CREATED_AT (the owning non-null keyset columns) execute as the
   real keyset sorts, deterministic with the id tiebreaker;
   START_DATE/END_DATE (the optional policy-window columns) answer
   the explicit not-implemented error.
  """
  promotions(
    "Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."
    after: String,
    "Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."
    before: String,
    "Retrieve the first n elements from the list."
    first: Int,
    "Retrieve the last n elements from the list."
    last: Int,
    "Sort promotions."
    sortBy: PromotionSortingInput,
    "Where filtering options for promotions."
    where: PromotionWhereInput
  ): PromotionCountableConnection
  service(id: ID!): Service
  """
   Forward-only keyset connection over ACTIVE catalog listings, ordered
   by createdAt DESC, id DESC. Cursors are opaque framework-generated
   positions and may be reused with a different first value because they
   identify a row's sort key, not an absolute offset. The configured
   default and hard maximum are owned by marketplace.graphql.pagination;
   do not add an SDL literal default that shadows that configuration.
  """
  services(after: String, first: Int): ServiceConnection!
  """
   "List of the shop's staff users." — the Saleor staff list with its
   countable-connection envelope (edges/pageInfo/totalCount, byte-shape
   from the pinned schema). FORWARD-ONLY keyset paging on this first
   slice: first/after ride the platform's ScrollPosition keyset
   contract (the storeProducts/services precedent — cursors identify a
   row's sort key (email|createdAt|updatedAt, id), never an absolute
   offset); before/last stay declared (the exact Saleor argument shape)
   but answer an explicit classified error until a backward scroll
   exists — a recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op. filter is
   likewise the declared wire shape with an explicit not-yet-supported
   error. Sort vocabulary is Saleor's full UserSortField enum; the
   fields with an owning indexed column (EMAIL/CREATED_AT/
   LAST_MODIFIED_AT) execute as real keyset sorts, the rest answer the
   same explicit error. MANAGE_STAFF on Saleor → ADMIN here.
  """
  staffUsers(
    "Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."
    after: String,
    "Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."
    before: String,
    "Filtering options for staff users."
    filter: StaffUserInput,
    "Retrieve the first n elements from the list."
    first: Int,
    "Retrieve the last n elements from the list."
    last: Int,
    "Sort staff users."
    sortBy: UserSortingInput
  ): UserCountableConnection
  """
   Dashboard's provider-owned catalog surface. This is a journey contract, not
   a mirror of the catalog tables; the fetchers delegate to ProductAdminSpi.
  """
  storeProduct(id: ID!): StoreProduct
  storeProductAttributeValues(productId: ID!): [StoreProductAttributeValue!]!
  storeProductTypes: [StoreProductType!]!
  storeProductVariantAttributeValues(variantId: ID!): [StoreProductAttributeValue!]!
  storeProductVariants(productId: ID!): [StoreProductVariant!]!
  """
   Forward-only keyset connection. Filter fields are limited to current domain
   attributes; the sort vocabulary is an allow-list backed by non-null indexed
   fields. Keep filter and sortBy identical when following an after cursor.
  """
  storeProducts(after: String, filter: StoreProductFilterInput, first: Int, sortBy: StoreProductSortInput): StoreProductConnection!
  """
   "Look up a user by ID or email address." — the Saleor wire shape
   carries id/email/externalReference; on this platform externalReference
   maps to the identity owner's subject (the OIDC subject IS the external
   account identifier of record — the same column the JWT sub joins).
   Requires one of MANAGE_STAFF/MANAGE_USERS/MANAGE_ORDERS on Saleor —
   enforced server-side as the platform's ADMIN capability at the
   identity use-case boundary (the RBAC mapping row of the divergence
   registry), never as a UI route guard.
  """
  user(email: String, externalReference: String, id: ID): User
  """
   === Campaign packet campaign-b3-a3 (integrated by A0 — the SDL steward) ===
   "Look up a voucher by ID or external reference." — the Saleor
   voucher lookup (MANAGE_DISCOUNTS → ADMIN here, enforced in the
   owning pricing use case). The id executes through the typed
   global-ID codec: an unknown but well-formed ID answers null (the
   safe absence); a malformed or mistyped global ID answers the
   codec's classified validation error — never a raw UUID fallback.
   externalReference (no external-ID column) and channel (no
   channel model — the PENDING-ADR row) stay declared (the exact
   Saleor argument shape) but answer an explicit classified error —
   a recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op.
  """
  voucher(
    "Slug of a channel for which the data should be returned (no channel model on this platform — an explicit classified error)."
    channel: String,
    "External ID of the voucher (no external-ID column on this platform — an explicit classified error)."
    externalReference: String,
    "ID of the voucher."
    id: ID
  ): Voucher
  """
   "List of the shop's vouchers." — the Saleor voucher list with its
   countable-connection envelope (edges/pageInfo/totalCount,
   byte-shape from the pinned schema). FORWARD-ONLY keyset paging on
   this first slice: first/after ride the platform's ScrollPosition
   keyset contract (the staffUsers/permissionGroups/productTypes
   precedent — cursors identify a row's sort key (code, id), never
   an absolute offset); before/last stay declared (the exact Saleor
   argument shape) but answer an explicit classified error until a
   backward scroll exists. filter, the deprecated query and channel
   are likewise the declared wire shape with an explicit
   not-yet-supported error. The sort vocabulary is Saleor's
   VoucherSortField enum: CODE (deprecated upstream) executes as the
   real keyset sort, deterministic with the id tiebreaker; every
   other field answers the explicit not-implemented error.
  """
  vouchers(
    "Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."
    after: String,
    "Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."
    before: String,
    "Slug of a channel for which the data should be returned."
    channel: String,
    "Filtering options for vouchers."
    filter: VoucherFilterInput,
    "Retrieve the first n elements from the list."
    first: Int,
    "Retrieve the last n elements from the list."
    last: Int,
    "Search vouchers by name or code."
    query: String @deprecated(reason : "Use `filter.search` input instead."),
    "Sort voucher."
    sortBy: VoucherSortingInput
  ): VoucherCountableConnection
}

