  """
  priceMinor: Int
  "ID of the product the variant registers under (typed global ID of the Product root's type)."
  product: ID!
  "The seller's own SKU (unique within the seller's namespace)."
  sku: String
}

"""
 Saleor's product-variant filter input — the declared wire shape of the
 filter argument (see productVariants: an explicit classified error
 until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: search and
 sku carry the scalar filter surface; metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
 closure), isPreorder (the deprecated preorder fact) and updatedAt
 (DateTimeRangeInput) stay undeclared until an owning capability exists
 — the same declared-shape rule the ProductTypeFilterInput precedents
 established.
"""
input ProductVariantFilterInput {
  search: String
  sku: [String!]
}

"""
 =====================================================================
 The bounded ProductVariantInput — the pinned Saleor input's OWNED
 movable set only: the SKU, the display name and the
 platform-extension price carrier (the row's own amendable facts —
 the entity's reviseDetails seam). The ownership facts (product,
 provider, currency — the denormalized copies), the reserved counter
 and the availability lifecycle are each their own owning
 capability, never an update side effect. Omitted (null) fields
 preserve the column.
 =====================================================================
"""
input ProductVariantInput {
  "The option's display name (null preserves)."
  name: String
  """
  PLATFORM EXTENSION: the authoritative unit price in minor units (a
  non-negative amount; null preserves the column).
  """
  priceMinor: Int
  "The seller's own SKU (null preserves; a new value must stay free in the seller's namespace)."
  sku: String
}

"""
 Saleor's product-variant sorting input — the full pinned vocabulary
 (upstream's own two values, verbatim): BOTH fields execute as the real
 forward-only keyset sorts (LAST_MODIFIED_AT over the entity's own
 non-null updated_at audit column, ID over the unique key), in both
 directions, deterministic with the id tiebreaker where the sort field
 is not already unique. direction reuses the EXISTING shared
 OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
"""
input ProductVariantSortingInput {
  "Specifies the direction in which to sort productVariants."
  direction: OrderDirection!
  "Sort productVariants by the selected field."
  field: ProductVariantSortField!
}

"""
 Saleor's product-variant where input — the declared wire shape of the
 where argument (see productVariants: an explicit classified error
 until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids
 carries the scalar filter surface; sku (its StringFilterInput closure),
 updatedAt (DateTimeRangeInput), metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
 closure), attributes (the AssignedAttributeWhereInput family) and the
 AND/OR combinators stay undeclared until an owning capability exists —
 any where use answers the classified not-implemented error before
 field-level semantics matter, and a Dashboard query naming an
 undeclared sub-field fails schema validation loudly (never a silent
 no-op).
"""
input ProductVariantWhereInput {
  ids: [ID!]
}

"""
 Saleor's product where input — the declared wire shape of the where
 argument (see products: an explicit classified error until the
 owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids carry the
 owned scalar facts; every other closure family stays undeclared
 until an owning capability exists — any where use answers the
 classified not-implemented error.
"""
input ProductWhereInput {
  ids: [ID!]
}

"""
 Saleor's promotion sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
 pinned enum is declared verbatim; NAME and CREATED_AT execute as
 the real forward-only keyset sorts (the owning non-null columns,
 id tiebreaker); START_DATE/END_DATE (the optional policy-window
 columns) answer the explicit not-implemented error. direction
 reuses the EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
"""
input PromotionSortingInput {
  "Specifies the direction in which to sort promotions."
  direction: OrderDirection!
  "Sort promotions by the selected field."
  field: PromotionSortField!
}

"""
 Saleor's promotion where-filter input — the declared wire shape of
 the where argument (see promotions: an explicit classified error
 until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids
 carries the scalar filter surface; name (its StringFilterInput
 closure), startDate/endDate (DateTimeFilterInput), isOldSale, type
 (PromotionTypeEnumFilterInput), metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
 closure) and the AND/OR combinators stay undeclared until an owning
 capability exists — any where use answers the classified
 not-implemented error before field-level semantics matter, and a
 Dashboard query naming an undeclared sub-field fails schema
 validation loudly (never a silent no-op).
"""
input PromotionWhereInput {
  ids: [ID!]
}

input ReorderInput {
  "The ID of the item to move (the context's own typed global ID)."
  id: ID!
  """
  The new relative sorting position of the item (from -inf to
  +inf). 1 moves the item one position forward, -1 moves the item
  one position backward, 0 leaves the item unchanged.
  """
  sortOrder: Int
}

input SeoInput {
  description: String
  title: String
}

"""
 Input speaks integer cents — the domain money language of every write
 surface (REST CreateListingRequest.priceCents, V2 price_cents >= 0,
 BookingInfo). DGS's DefaultInputObjectMapper binds input keys to Java
 record components BY NAME, so the field name must equal the
 ServiceInput.priceCents record component (the same by-name contract the
 spring-graphql binder enforced before the Phase-2 migration). (The read
 side keeps display units: Service.price — major units via
 ServiceMapper.) Int is a signed 32-bit scalar per the GraphQL spec —
 the explicit shared ceiling 2,147,483,647 is declared in ServiceInput
 via @Max and enforced by the fetcher's explicit Bean Validation.
"""
input ServiceInput {
  category: String!
  description: String
  name: String!
  priceCents: Int!
}

input StaffCreateInput {
  addGroups: [ID!]
  email: String
  firstName: String
  isActive: Boolean
  lastName: String
  redirectUrl: String
}

input StaffNotificationRecipientInput {
  active: Boolean
  email: String
  user: ID
}

input StaffUpdateInput {
  addGroups: [ID!]
  email: String
  firstName: String
  isActive: Boolean
  lastName: String
  removeGroups: [ID!]
}

"""
 Saleor's staff-user filter input — the declared wire shape of the
 filter argument (see staffUsers: an explicit classified error until
 the owning query capability exists).
"""
input StaffUserInput {
  ids: [ID!]
  search: String
  status: StaffMemberStatus
}

input StoreProductAttributeValueInput {
  assignmentId: ID!
  booleanValue: Boolean
  numberValue: String
  optionId: ID
  textValue: String
}

"""
 priceMinor must be a non-negative, base-10 integer string (for example "149900").
 Domain services remain authoritative for ownership, ProductType rules and publishability.
"""
input StoreProductCreateInput {
  currency: String!
  description: String
  priceMinor: String!
  productTypeId: ID
  storeCategoryCode: String!
  title: String!
}

"""
 Adapted to the catalog fields the platform actually owns. Prices are minor-unit
 decimal strings to avoid GraphQL Int/Float precision loss. Bounds and PRICE_MINOR
 sorting require currency because priceMinor values across currencies are incomparable.
"""
input StoreProductFilterInput {
  currency: String
  maxPriceMinor: String
  minPriceMinor: String
  productTypeId: ID
  search: String
  status: StoreProductStatus
  storeCategoryCode: String
}

input StoreProductSortInput {
  direction: StoreProductSortDirection! = DESC
  field: StoreProductSortField! = CREATED_AT
}

input StoreProductUpdateInput {
  description: String
  priceMinor: String!
  title: String!
}

input StoreProductVariantCreateInput {
  attributeValues: [StoreProductAttributeValueInput!]!
  name: String
  priceMinor: String!
  sku: String!
}

input StringFilterInput {
  eq: String
  oneOf: [String!]
}

"""
 =====================================================================
 The bounded TranslationInput — the pinned Saleor input's OWNED field
 set only: the display name (the registry's bilingual column family).
 The unowned members (description/fullDescription as JSONString,
 slug/seoTitle/seoDescription) have no owning capabilities on this
 surface and stay undeclared — recorded divergences, never faked.
 =====================================================================
"""
input TranslationInput {
  "The addressed language's display name (null preserves the column)."
  name: String
}

input UserCreateInput {
  channel: String
  customerType: ID
  defaultBillingAddress: AddressInput
  defaultShippingAddress: AddressInput
  email: String
  firstName: String
  isActive: Boolean
  lastName: String
  redirectUrl: String
}

"""
 Saleor's user sorting input and field vocabulary (full closure; the
 subset with an owning column executes — EMAIL/CREATED_AT/
 LAST_MODIFIED_AT — the rest answer the explicit not-supported error).
"""
input UserSortingInput {
  "Specifies the direction in which to sort users."
  direction: OrderDirection!
  "Sort users by the selected field."
  field: UserSortField!
}

"""
 Saleor's voucher filter input — the declared wire shape of the
 filter argument (see vouchers: an explicit classified error until
 the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: search/ids
 carry the scalar filter surface; status (DiscountStatusEnum list),
 timesUsed (IntRangeInput), discountType (VoucherDiscountType list),
 started (DateTimeRangeInput) and metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
 closure) stay undeclared until an owning capability exists — the
 same declared-shape rule the StaffUserInput/ProductTypeFilterInput
 precedents established.
"""
input VoucherFilterInput {
  ids: [ID!]
  search: String
}

"""
 Unowned Saleor members stay undeclared (recorded divergences): the
 voucher-type discrimination (VoucherTypeEnum — no column), the
 addCodes feature-preview codes model, the catalogue scoping family
 (products/variants/collections/categories), minCheckoutItemsQuantity
 (no owner), countries (no shipping owner), applyOncePerOrder,
 onlyForStaff, singleUse.
 =====================================================================
"""
input VoucherInput {
  "Voucher should be applied once per customer."
  applyOncePerCustomer: Boolean
  "Code to use the voucher (4..64 uppercase letters/digits/dashes)."
  code: String
  "PLATFORM EXTENSION: the row's ISO-4217 currency denomination."
  currency: String
  """
  PLATFORM EXTENSION (the row's NOT NULL discount policy — no Saleor
  carrier in the declarable closure): PERCENTAGE vouchers carry
  1..10000 basis points; FIXED vouchers carry the minor amount.
  """
  discountValue: Int
  "Choices: fixed or percentage."
  discountValueType: DiscountValueTypeEnum
  "End date of the voucher in ISO 8601 format."
  endDate: String
  "PLATFORM EXTENSION: the minimum spend in minor units (>= 0; omitted defaults to 0)."
  minSpend: Int
  "Voucher name."
  name: String
  "Start date of the voucher in ISO 8601 format."
  startDate: String
  "Limit number of times this voucher can be used in total (or null for unlimited)."
  usageLimit: Int
}

"""
 Saleor's voucher sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
 pinned enum is declared verbatim (CODE deprecated upstream with no
 reason string in the pinned schema); CODE executes as the real
 forward-only keyset sort (the row's non-null normalized code, id
 tiebreaker); NAME/START_DATE/END_DATE (optional columns),
 VALUE/MINIMUM_SPENT_AMOUNT (channel-scoped money upstream + the
 frozen money contract), TYPE (no voucher-type discrimination) and
 USAGE_LIMIT (optional column) answer the explicit not-implemented
 error, as does the deprecated nested channel. direction reuses the
 EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
"""
input VoucherSortingInput {
  "Specifies the channel in which to sort the data."
  channel: String @deprecated(reason : "Use root-level channel argument instead.")
  "Specifies the direction in which to sort vouchers."
  direction: OrderDirection!
  "Sort vouchers by the selected field."
  field: VoucherSortField!
}
